    "title": "Baton Rouge library hosts 'Nine-to-Five' Day to honor Dolly Parton's legacy - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WBRZ Staff ,\n1 days ago BATON ROUGE — Dozens of people gathered at the Main Library on Goodwood to celebrate the legacy of late country music star Dolly Parton. The non-profit Dolly Diamonds hosted the event, called \"Nine-to-Five\" Day. Guests danced to her iconic songs and participated in a Dolly look-a-like contest. They also... Read full article",
